config KB_HFXO_ALWAYS_ON
    bool "Keep the 32 MHz crystal (HFXO) running"
    depends on CLOCK_CONTROL_NRF
    help
      Hold a permanent request on the nRF high-frequency clock so the 32 MHz
      crystal never stops. The ESB TDMA stack switches HFXO off between slots
      and turns it back on only ~366 us before the next RX window (Nordic's own
      MPSL budgets 1400 us), so a slow crystal can miss slots and skew the drift
      estimate, which desyncs the half. Costs roughly 0.25 mA while awake; the
      clock stops anyway when the half enters deep sleep.
